# Root-level ignore rules. The app lives in Black-Eclipse-site/ and has its own
# detailed .gitignore; these cover the git repository root only.

# SQLite database files (WAL mode) anywhere in the tree. The previous patterns
# were the literal strings `0`, `0-shm`, `0-wal` (a truncated `*.db`), which
# matched any path segment named `0` and could silently ignore a real file.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Local, regenerable artifacts kept at the repository root.
# A stray root `node_modules/` can appear if a tool (e.g. vitest) runs from the
# repo root instead of Black-Eclipse-site/; it is build cache, never committed.
node_modules/
/_backups/
/opencode/
